SUMMARY:Survivalist Series: Introduction to Navigation
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/intro-navigation-26)**\n\n
 **Navigation isn’t a lost art - it’s a life-saving skill. Whether you
 ’re exploring remote backcountry or just trying to orient yourself on a 
 trail\, knowing how to read the land can make all the difference.**\n\nJoi
 n us for this *one-day navigation workshop\,* which will equip you with th
 e skills needed for safe and confident adventures.\n\n**Interested in join
 ing this year’s Epics? Completing this and other relevant courses will s
 upport your approval process for advanced adventures.**\n\n**Morning: Theo
 ry**\nWe’ll start with hot beverages and a hands-on classroom session wh
 ere you’ll learn:\n\n* Why maps still matter in a GPS world\n* How to re
 ad a topo map and visualize the land\n* What contours tell you about your 
 route (and your legs)\n* How to orient yourself when you’re turned aroun
 d\n* Compass skills that could save your life\n\n**Afternoon: Practice**\n
 After a quick lunch\, the real fun begins. With only a map\, compass\, and
  your brain\, you’ll work in teams to complete a real-world navigation c
 hallenge. Each team gets a unique course and a grid reference sheet to plo
 t and follow. Fastest (and most accurate) team earns top bragging rights a
 s Wilderness Union’s best navigators.\n\nYou’ll build and follow a rou
 te card\, learn to trust your instincts\, and develop the kind of confiden
 ce that only comes with practice.\n\n**Your Instructor:** Former Canadian 
 Army Advanced Reconnaissance Instructor\, Captain Buckingham is a decorate
 d Pathfinder and the Canadian Infantry School’s top navigation instructo
 r\, he’ll guide you every step of the way.\n\n**Who It’s For:** This c
 ourse is for beginners and intermediate explorers alike. No military minds
 et required—just curiosity\, a willingness to learn\, and a love of gett
 ing outside. This is an amazing opportunity not only to learn from a world
 -class expert but it's a fun\, practical lesson at a uniquely low price.\n
 \n**About this series:** The Survivalist Series is an expert-led set of co
 urses designed to develop applicable\, and life-saving skills in the wilde
 rness. Keep your eyes peeled for more courses that become available.\n\n**
 Due to the cost of parking at Bronte Creek\, WU transport is recommended f
 or this course.**\n\n**Highlights**\n**Expert Instruction -** Our amazing 
 expert guides will teach you everything you need to know in a safe and fun
  way.\n**Practical Skills -** Develop essential skills to survive and thri
 ve in the wild.\n‍**Local Adventure -** Just 45 minutes from Toronto\, t
 his adventure is close to home for anyone living in the GTA.\n\n**Event co
 st: $80+HST - optional transport available.**\n**Register [here.](https://
 www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/intro-navigation-26)**\n\n**About Wilde
 rness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors c
 ommunity that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and 
 helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The gro
 up is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and 
 abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event att
 endance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large e
 nough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not over
 whelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https:
 //www.wildernessunion.com/)***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/314285565/
